/* A short front door to the existing reproducible analysis. */
(()=>{'use strict';const D=window.AceEvidence.data,money=n=>new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US',{style:'currency',currency:'USD',maximumFractionDigits:0}).format(n);
const panel=document.createElement('section');panel.id='findingsOverview';panel.tabIndex=-1;panel.setAttribute('aria-labelledby','findingsTitle');
panel.innerHTML=`<div class="findings-heading"><span class="sim-eyebrow">DASHBOARD ROYALE · THE ACTUAL CHALLENGE</span><h1 id="findingsTitle">Our Casino Findings</h1><p>The manager wants to replace the ten lowest-earning machines. We checked whether the real problem was <b>luck, location or a leak.</b></p><p class="findings-scope">Organizer’s synthetic casino data · January–June 2025 · July 1–30 action plan</p></div>
<section class="findings-decision"><span class="findings-number">01 / OUR DECISION</span><h2>Inspect one. Keep the reserve.</h2><p>Fund a <strong>$1,200 inspection of M-1158</strong> and hold <strong>$98,800</strong>. Low earnings alone do not justify replacing all ten machines.</p><details class="decision-reason"><summary>Why not just wait—or replace it?</summary><div class="decision-options"><p><b>Wait · $0 now</b><br>Avoids spending, but leaves a specific payout/configuration discrepancy unresolved.</p><p><b>Inspect · $1,200</b><br>Checks the discrepancy before a larger commitment. May find nothing; the value is information, not guaranteed recovery.</p><p><b>Replace one machine · $22,000</b><br>Much larger commitment. The current evidence does not establish that replacement fixes the cause or pays for itself.</p></div><p><b>Decision rule:</b> reconcile meters and payout settings first. If no fault is verified, monitor. Authorize any repair only after a separate quote and review; compare subsequent operation with same-game peers and track property-wide contribution after costs.</p><small>Prices: organizer action catalogue. No probability of a fault or expected ROI is estimated here.</small></details><div class="findings-actions"><button data-desk="brief">See all ten decisions →</button><button data-desk="plan">Check the $100,000 plan →</button></div><small>Inspection may find nothing. Recovery and repair costs are uncertain; the plan includes a measurement approach.</small></section>
<section class="findings-why"><span class="findings-number">02 / WHY</span><h2>Four things changed the answer.</h2><div class="findings-grid">
<article><span>♠ MACHINES</span><h3>Low totals can be misleading.</h3><p>Compare opportunity to earn and expected payouts. Short exposure, quiet locations and luck can all look like a bad machine.</p><button data-desk="machines">Compare machines & dates →</button></article>
<article><span>♦ LOCATION</span><h3>One mover improved. Not all four.</h3><p>One of four movers improved relative to similar stayers. Back Forty was already declining before its closure. Neither pattern proves new casino-wide profit.</p><button data-desk="movers">See the four moves →</button></article>
<article><span>♥ DOWNTIME</span><h3>A broken slot can lose play.</h3><p>But some customers use another machine. Change that assumption to see the difference between machine losses and whole-casino losses.</p><button data-desk="operations">Explore downtime & switching →</button></article>
<article><span>♣ GUESTS & COMPS</span><h3>Check both sides of the ledger.</h3><p>Tracked players wagered $163.8M and received $148.2M. The top 10% accounted for 63.8% of expected loss. Loyalty redemptions cost $190,669; points pricing changed in late April. These figures cover carded play, not everyone.</p><button data-desk="guests">Explore guests & loyalty costs →</button></article></div></section>
<section class="findings-check"><span class="findings-number">03 / CHECK OUR WORK</span><h2>Evidence you can inspect.</h2><p>Our weekday forecast’s average error was <b>${money(D.forecast.maeWeekday)}</b>, versus <b>${money(D.forecast.maeBaseline)}</b> for the simple baseline. January–April trained the model; May–June tested it. It informs when to schedule disruption—not whether an inspection will pay off.</p><div class="findings-actions"><button data-desk="forecast">Model & validation →</button><a href="evidence/CLAIMS_AND_EVIDENCE.md">Claims, limitations & AI use ↗</a><button data-evidence="plan">Inspection measurement plan →</button><a href="evidence/PILOT_PROTOCOL.md">Optional pilot protocol ↗</a><a href="evidence/source.zip">Download code ↓</a><a href="dashboard.html">Full analytical dashboard ↗</a></div></section>
<p class="findings-boundary">Want to try managing a floor? <a href="#game">Play Casino Manager</a>. Its simplified economy is fictional; gameplay earnings are not results from this analysis.</p>`;
document.getElementById('floor').prepend(panel);
window.AceFindings={enter(){document.body.dataset.findingsPanel='overview';document.getElementById('evidenceWorkspace').open=false;panel.focus({preventScroll:true});}};
})();
